# M0: parameters that exist only on the MS-ADPCM path.  Kept apart from the
# shared model so a tuning run on an IMA-only corpus cannot quietly drift them.

Prefix M0
Debug 1
Const 0

# iDelta has no small index the way the IMA step has, so it is read in the log
# domain -- the octave plus MS_DLOG_SUB bits below the leading one -- and this
# threshold map decides how many of those steps become separate contexts.  It
# can be fine where iDelta discriminates and coarse where it does not, which no
# single shift can express.  Its LENGTH is tied to MS_DLOG_SUB in the .cpp:
# ((EMAX-E0)<<SUB)+(1<<SUB) input positions must be covered.
Index Md
 d0: dlog, 1!011011011010101001010001011010000000000000000000000000000000000000000000

# Bit-tree order for the MS nibble: 0 raw two's complement, 1 sign then
# magnitude, 2 magnitude then sign.  The code is a quantized residual, so the
# natural split is not obvious -- this was measured, not reasoned.
Number MSMAP, 1, 0!00

# Confidence rule: 0 keeps the SIGN of where the prediction sat inside its
# quantizer cell, 1 keeps only the distance.  MS rounds to nearest, so the sign
# says which neighbour is the near miss; worth 0.48% when it was measured.
Number MSCONF, 1, 0!0

# Decay of the two iDelta-predictor cost trackers.  Encoders differ: ffmpeg
# carries its running iDelta across block boundaries, others re-fit per block,
# and the per-channel choice is made by decayed absolute error.
Number MSDSH, 1, 0!00101
